# Django DB Patterns

- Tenant models (`reporting`, `cost_models`) require `schema_context` / `tenant_context` — see [multi-tenancy.mdc](multi-tenancy.mdc)
- Prefer `select_related` / `prefetch_related` to avoid N+1 queries
- Use transactions for multi-step writes; bulk ops for large inserts/updates
- Timezone-aware datetimes only
- Partitioned tables: Django `on_delete` is unreliable — use `cascade_delete()` from `koku/koku/database.py`
- Mixed-type ORM aggregations need explicit `output_field` (see [`docs/agent/backend-gotchas.md`](../../docs/agent/backend-gotchas.md))
